    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: a0b6bd8152ae9584381dd43e9d27c0619c141cca -->\n**Ready for the maintainer to merge.**\n\nTest-only: one new suite (`crates/app/tests/bore_entry.rs`) and one decision file. No product code, goldens, snapshot PNGs, build.rs, dependencies or process files changed. Merges cleanly with current origin/main.\n\n**What looks good**\n- Each test asserts what the body says. The undrilled 8 mm non-centre-cutting bore is ramped, not plunged: `first_solid_plunge` (`plunge_law`) returns `None`, and the note `NOT_CENTER_CUTTING` with \"ramp along the first cut\" is checked. The 9 mm hole is refused with the specific `CENTER_CUT_REFUSAL` constant, not a bare `is_err()`.\n- The control test (`a_centre_cutting_cutter_keeps_its_axial_plunge`) shows the same audit convicts the centre-cutting path, so the NC pass is not a blind audit.\n- The assertions are specific enough to fail if the law were removed: without it, the NC path would contain an axial plunge into solid, which `first_solid_plunge` finds, and the note and refusal string would not appear.\n- Provenance line and Gate map header are present. No `VerifyContext` is built by hand. Body has `Changelog: none` and `Refs #1036`.\n\n**Local results** (worktree at a0b6bd81, trial merge with origin/main clean)\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test bore_entry` | 3 passed, 0 failed |\n| `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --tests -- -D warnings` | clean |\n\n**Notes (not blocking)**\n1. The task asked that a pre-drilled hole passes; no test in this file covers that case. The body does not claim it, and the body's \"not exercised\" list does not mention it either. If it is meant to be pinned, add one test with a `Hole` on a pre-drilled column (or a footprint in `Solid`).\n2. The mutation check (removing the law and watching these fail) was reasoned from the assertions, not run, since it needs a product-code edit in the worktree.\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
